    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196-a1">

                <pb facs="0309" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg235"/>

                <head>[Circular.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department Of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 12, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It has come to the knowledge of this
                    department that the governor of one of the States of the United States has
                    issued instruments signed by himself, and bearing the seal of the State over
                    which he presides, which instruments purport to be passports to citizens of the
                    United States. These proceedings having been brought to the attention of the
                    President of the United States, I am directed by Urn to inform the governors of
                    the several States that the granting of passports by them, or by any other State
                    authorities, is deemed to be in contravention of the Constitution and laws of
                    the United States and of the law of nations, and that all such instruments are
                    illegal and void, and that such instruments will in no case be recognized by
                    this department, or accepted or recognized by the governments of foreign
                    states.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your excellency’s obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Governor Of The State Of
                            —</hi>.</p>
                    <p>The same to all the governors of States.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
